      "id": "web-ui",
      "name": "Web UI",
      "type": "frontend"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "FastAPI backend (api/) that serves the static React bundle and exposes the wizard REST routes. Orchestrates the pipeline: PDF upload → truth extraction → job tailoring → guardrail validation → render/download. Configured entirely from env / .env at container start (no secrets entered in the UI)."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1783591752373-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Python",
                "FastAPI",
                "Uvicorn"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1783591752477-1",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "routes": [
                {
                  "desc": "LLM extracts structured truth.yaml from the uploaded PDF text.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/extract"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Return the current truth.yaml for the Review step.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/api/truth"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Save user corrections to truth.yaml (Review step); after this it is trusted.",
                  "method": "PUT",
                  "path": "/api/truth"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Extract posting keywords and produce an id-referenced tailored draft; returns any inferences needing confirmation.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/tailor"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Approve/reject inferred claims; approved ones are written back into truth.yaml as source:user-confirmed.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/confirm-inferences"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Guardrail-check the draft then render PDF/DOCX. On block, returns blockedClaims:[{claimId,experienceId,text,tokens[]}] (whole flagged bullets, not loose tokens; keeps unverifiable[] for back-compat). Accepts optional approvals:{approvedClaimIds[],deniedClaimIds[]} — approved claims count as allowed for THIS render only (no truth.yaml write), denied claims are dropped from the draft.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/render"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Generate a guardrail-truthful cover letter (tone, length). Returns {blocked, unverifiable, pdfUrl, docxUrl}; blocked if any factual claim fails truth validation.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/cover-letter"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Saved-profile status ({hasProfile}) so the wizard can offer \"use saved profile\" and skip re-upload.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/api/profile"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Download a rendered artifact (CV/cover-letter PDF or DOCX) by filename.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/api/download/{name}"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Return the canonical ATS screening answers stored in truth.answers.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/api/profile/answers"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Partially update the canonical ATS screening answers in truth.answers; returns the merged answers.",
                  "method": "PUT",
                  "path": "/api/profile/answers"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Delete many screenings in one call; reports per-id outcomes. Operator-only — not an agent route and not an MCP tool.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/screenings/deletions"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Upload a CV as PDF, DOCX, TXT or Markdown (multipart); backend extracts text per format and stores the file under its own extension.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/upload"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 240,
            "id": "widget-1783591770368-2",
            "title": "Wizard routes",
            "type": "endpoints",
            "w": 440,
            "x": 90,
            "y": 90
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "vars": [
                {
                  "desc": "Which provider implementation to use.",
                  "example": "anthropic | openai | ollama",
                  "key": "LLM_PROVIDER"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Model id (provider-specific).",
                  "example": "claude-3-5-sonnet",
                  "key": "LLM_MODEL"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "BYO key, used when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic.",
                  "example": "sk-ant-...",
                  "key": "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "BYO key, used when LLM_PROVIDER=openai.",
                  "example": "sk-...",
                  "key": "OPENAI_API_KEY"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Ollama endpoint, used when LLM_PROVIDER=ollama.",
                  "example": "http://ollama:11434",
                  "key": "OLLAMA_HOST"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Fernet master key (URL-safe base64, 32 bytes) that encrypts saved provider API keys in ./data/secrets.enc. Generate via `python -m api.genkey`. Missing/invalid disables the secrets feature (falls back to env-var credentials).",
                  "example": "aQ2mA0m3wF6b8xk2s9v0Xr7uY1zC4dN6pQ8rS0tU2w=",
                  "key": "ENCRYPTION_KEY"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Directory of the built React bundle to serve.",
                  "example": "api/static",
                  "key": "STATIC_DIR"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Comma-separated allowed CORS origins.",
                  "example": "http://localhost:5173",
                  "key": "CORS_ORIGINS"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Port the Uvicorn server binds to.",
                  "example": "8000",
                  "key": "PORT"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Path to the mounted data volume (truth.yaml, secrets.enc, profile.pdf).",
                  "example": "./data",
                  "key": "DATA_DIR"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Host-side port the compose stack publishes the UI on (docker-compose.yml ${APP_PORT:-5627}). Display only — the app still binds PORT (8080) inside the container. Read by api.config.public_url() to print a reachable URL at startup. Unset in local dev, where it falls back to PORT.",
                  "example": "8123",
                  "key": "PUBLIC_PORT"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1783591787714-3",
            "title": "Configuration & Environment",
            "type": "config",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "routes": [
                {
                  "desc": "Provider settings status (encryptionAvailable, activeProvider, model, *KeySet booleans, ollamaHost). Never returns raw secrets.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/api/settings"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Save provider selection + API key/model/host; encrypts to ./data/secrets.enc via ENCRYPTION_KEY. Empty apiKey leaves the stored key unchanged.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/settings"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Test connection: a tiny live provider call with saved/submitted credentials. Returns {ok, detail}.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/settings/test"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "List available models for a provider (live model-list lookup).",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/models"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 240,
            "id": "widget-1783598621851-5",
            "title": "Settings routes",
            "type": "endpoints",
            "w": 440,
            "x": 180,
            "y": 180
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "POST /api/render accepts optional approvals:{approvedClaimIds[],deniedClaimIds[]}. On a guardrail block it returns blockedClaims:[{claimId,experienceId,text,tokens[]}] — each a whole draft bullet that tripped the guardrail. Approving a claim makes its text allowed for THAT render only (merged into the matching scope's allowed set before guardrail.validate); denying drops the bullet from the rendered draft. Approvals must NOT be persisted to truth.yaml (write_confirmed is NOT used here) because the user generates many tailored CVs/cover letters from one immutable truth file. claimId is a deterministic hash of experienceId+text so the frontend can round-trip decisions."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1783610638800-5",
            "title": "Render-scoped approvals (no truth write)",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 180,
            "y": 180
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "POST /api/confirm-inferences accepts approved:[{id, claim, experienceId}] so a user-edited claim (and re-targeted experience) at Step 4 is what gets written as the user-confirmed bullet. approvedIds:[string] is still accepted as a deprecated fallback (writes the original draft claim). write_confirmed persists the supplied claim text verbatim."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1783613369039-6",
            "title": "Editable inferences at Confirm",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 210,
            "y": 210
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "routes": [
                {
                  "desc": "List all tracked job applications.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/api/applications"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Create a new application record.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/api/applications"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Update an application record (fields and status flags).",
                  "method": "PUT",
                  "path": "/api/applications/{id}"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Delete an application and its owned document files.",
                  "method": "DELETE",
                  "path": "/api/applications/{id}"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Save edited CV content for an application and re-render its pdf/docx (guardrail-checked).",
                  "method": "PUT",
                  "path": "/api/applications/{id}/cv"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Save edited cover-letter content for an application and re-render its pdf/docx.",
                  "method": "PUT",
                  "path": "/api/applications/{id}/cover-letter"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 240,
            "id": "widget-1783684105808-7",
            "title": "Application routes",
            "type": "endpoints",
            "w": 440,
            "x": 40,
            "y": 40
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "POST /api/render and POST /api/cover-letter accept an optional applicationId. When present, the rendered output is saved as the named application's owned CV/cover-letter document (per-application filenames, e.g. cv_<appId>.pdf) instead of overwriting the shared cv.pdf/cover_letter.pdf. Absent applicationId preserves today's behavior (scratch preview files). Applications may have no posting (General submissions)."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1783684115321-8",
            "title": "Attach output to an application",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 70,
            "y": 70
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "POST /api/render returns the rendered CV HTML as `html`, and POST /api/cover-letter returns the generated letter as `text`. These expose the generated content so the Web UI can pre-fill an editor; the user edits and saves it back via the guardrail-checked PUT /api/applications/{id}/cv (html) and .../cover-letter (text) routes."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1783685376757-9",
            "title": "Editable generated source",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 100,
            "y": 100
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "When attaching a document to an application (PUT /api/applications/{id}/cv, PUT /api/applications/{id}/cover-letter) or rendering to an application (POST /api/render, POST /api/cover-letter with applicationId), the guardrail runs first and the document SOURCE is saved before rendering. If WeasyPrint (PDF) and pandoc (DOCX) are both unavailable, no file is produced and download URLs are null — but the save still succeeds. Responses carry renderUnavailable:true in that case so the UI can report \"saved to the application, but its PDF/DOCX couldn't be generated in this environment (install the render backend / run the Docker image)\". Do NOT treat renderUnavailable as a save failure."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1784025108420-10",
            "title": "renderUnavailable flag on saves",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 130,
            "y": 130
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "POST /api/cover-letter accepts an optional approvals:{approvedClaimIds, deniedClaimIds}. Approved claim texts are added to the guardrail's allowed set for THIS generation only (no truth.yaml write); denied claims are dropped before rendering. When blocked, the response returns grouped blockedClaims:[{claimId, text, tokens}] (same shape as POST /api/render) so the UI can offer per-claim approve/decline and re-check, instead of only a flat unverifiable token list."
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1784038212055-11",
            "title": "Render-scoped approvals for cover letters (no truth write)",
            "type": "note",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 160,
            "y": 160
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "routes": [
                {
