      "id": "application-tracker",
      "name": "Application Tracker",
      "type": "backend"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "Unattended job-application agent running as its OWN container (agent/Dockerfile, the `agent` compose service), separate from the app image so a crash there can never take the wizard down. entrypoint.sh preflights credentials and the selected browser driver, then execs supervisor.js, an always-on scheduler plus token-guarded control server that invokes agent/daily-apply.sh — which drives the headless `claude` CLI (@anthropic-ai/claude-code) against agent/prompt.md, agent/RUNBOOK.md and the MCP servers in agent/mcp.json. Schedule, enablement, job profiles and LLM credentials are fetched from the app's /api/agent/* config API (agent/agent-config.js); RUN_AT/RUN_DAYS env are only the fallback. The image is deliberately browserless: pages are rendered by the sibling `browser` service over HTTP MCP (default) or by the operator's host Chrome via the opt-in `interceptor` driver."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1787566001330-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Docker (separate image)",
                "Node 22",
                "Bash",
                "claude CLI (@anthropic-ai/claude-code)",
                "MCP",
                "jq"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1787566002714-1",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "routes": [
                {
                  "desc": "Trigger a run immediately, fire-and-forget. Requires X-Agent-Token matching AGENT_API_TOKEN.",
                  "method": "POST",
                  "path": "/run"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "{running, lastStartedAt, lastFinishedAt, lastExitCode}. Requires X-Agent-Token.",
                  "method": "GET",
                  "path": "/status"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 240,
            "id": "widget-1787566004099-2",
            "title": "Control server (supervisor.js)",
            "type": "endpoints",
            "w": 440,
            "x": 90,
            "y": 90
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "vars": [
                {
                  "desc": "App MCP endpoint; also the base for the /api/agent/* config and credential calls.",
                  "example": "http://app:8000/mcp",
                  "key": "TRUTHCV_MCP_URL"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Shared secret guarding the control server and forwarded as X-Agent-Token when fetching LLM credentials.",
                  "example": "<shared secret>",
                  "key": "AGENT_API_TOKEN"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Optional; when unset, credentials are fetched from the app at run time.",
                  "example": "sk-ant-...",
                  "key": "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "'browser' (default, sibling Chromium/@playwright/mcp service) or 'interceptor' (host Chrome, opt-in overlay).",
                  "example": "browser",
                  "key": "AGENT_BROWSER_DRIVER"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "HTTP MCP endpoint of the browser service.",
                  "example": "http://browser:8931/mcp",
                  "key": "BROWSER_MCP_URL"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Fallback schedule slots (HH:MM, container TZ) when the app config API is unreachable.",
                  "example": "09:00,15:00",
                  "key": "RUN_AT"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Fallback allowed weekdays (1=Mon..7=Sun).",
                  "example": "1,2,3,4,5",
                  "key": "RUN_DAYS"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Run once immediately and exit with the run's status.",
                  "example": "1",
                  "key": "RUN_ONCE"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Port the control server listens on (default 9099).",
                  "example": "9099",
                  "key": "AGENT_CONTROL_PORT"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Container timezone the schedule is interpreted in.",
                  "example": "Europe/London",
                  "key": "TZ"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1787566005511-3",
            "title": "Configuration & Environment",
            "type": "config",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "application-agent",
      "name": "Application Agent",
      "type": "backend"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "External Google service used for the Gmail connection: the OAuth 2.0 browser flow (accounts.google.com authorize, oauth2.googleapis.com/token for the PKCE code exchange and refresh-token renewal) and the Gmail REST API (gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/profile) read to identify the connected mailbox. Reached over HTTPS with httpx from connections/auth/gmail.py; tokens are persisted via the Secret Store."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1787568269048-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Google OAuth 2.0 (PKCE, offline access)",
                "Gmail REST API v1",
                "httpx"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1787568272749-1",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "gmail-api",
      "name": "Gmail / Google OAuth API",
      "type": "custom"
    },
    {
      "canvas": {
        "widgets": [
          {
            "data": {
              "text": "Provider connection layer (connections/): a static catalog of provider connection cards (catalog.py — claude, codex, openrouter, ollama) plus per-vendor auth flows under connections/auth/. connections/auth/gmail.py owns the Gmail OAuth flow end to end: start_login builds the Google authorize URL (PKCE S256, offline access, gmail.readonly scope), complete_login exchanges the code, reads the account's email from the Gmail profile API and stores the token record; get_valid_access_token refreshes lazily behind a lock with a 300s expiry skew; mark_reconnect_required blanks the tokens and flags reauthRequired when access is revoked. Credentials are never held here — every record is persisted through secretstore.get_connection/set_connection."
            },
            "h": 180,
            "id": "widget-1787568456174-0",
            "title": "Intent & Scope Description",
            "type": "text",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 30,
            "y": 30
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "techs": [
                "Python",
                "httpx",
                "Google OAuth 2.0 (PKCE)"
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1787568457598-1",
            "title": "Tech Stack Profiles",
            "type": "techstack",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 60,
            "y": 60
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "vars": [
                {
                  "desc": "Google OAuth client id; Gmail login/refresh fails with AuthError when unset.",
                  "example": "1234567890-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com",
                  "key": "GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID"
                },
                {
                  "desc": "Google OAuth client secret used for the code exchange and refresh calls.",
                  "example": "GOCSPX-…",
                  "key": "GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 200,
            "id": "widget-1787568459083-2",
            "title": "Configuration & Environment",
            "type": "config",
            "w": 350,
            "x": 90,
            "y": 90
          },
          {
            "data": {
              "fields": [
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "accessToken",
                  "notes": "Current Gmail access token; blanked when reconnect is required.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "refreshToken",
                  "notes": "Offline refresh token; carried over when Google omits it on refresh.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "expiresAt",
                  "notes": "Refreshed lazily once within 300s of expiry.",
                  "type": "float (epoch seconds)"
                },
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "scope",
                  "notes": "Defaults to https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "connectedAt",
                  "notes": "Preserved across refreshes.",
                  "type": "float (epoch seconds)"
                },
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "email",
                  "notes": "Account address read from the Gmail profile endpoint at login.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "flags": "-",
                  "name": "reauthRequired",
                  "notes": "Set by mark_reconnect_required when refresh is rejected.",
                  "type": "bool"
                }
              ]
            },
            "h": 240,
            "id": "widget-1787568460579-3",
            "title": "gmail connection record (secretstore \"gmail\".oauth)",
            "type": "schema",
            "w": 440,
            "x": 120,
            "y": 120
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "connections",
      "name": "Connections",
      "type": "backend"
    },
